# Curated routing-eval cases — Phase 0 of ARCHITECTURE_IMPROVEMENT_PLAN.md (§3.5, §9.2).
# One JSON object per line. Lines starting with '#' and blank lines are ignored.
# Schema: {"id": str, "prompt": str, "expect": [skill-id...], "reject": [skill-id...], "tags": [str...]}
#   - expect non-empty  => POSITIVE case: any listed skill is a correct top route (P@1/MRR/Recall@5).
#   - expect empty       => NEGATIVE/abstention case: the router should NOT route (or not to `reject`).
# Every id here is a verified canonical skill in manifest.json. `expect` is a human ground-truth
# label of the correct skill; the committed baseline records what the CURRENT router does against it,
# so paraphrase cases the lexical router currently misses are intentional — they quantify the recall
# gap Phase 1 (semantic routing) must close WITHOUT regressing the exact-name cases below.
#
# --- Exact name / alias (deterministic guardrail; should route) -------------------------------
